{
  "name": "Mac is offline: the phone holds the goal, then sends it when the Mac is back (SPEC-09 r15)",
  "notes": [
    "The relay answers targetOffline, so the phone shows the Other device offline copy and keeps the goal itself; the relay never holds it.",
    "While a goal is queued the phone pings the Mac; targetOffline means it is still away.",
    "The Mac's toolList on connect tells the phone it is back. The goal was spoken 3 hours earlier, so the phone asks again first, and sends it with a new command id once the user says yes."
